1. **A system for providing location-specific content to a mobile device, the system comprising:**

an indoor beacon configured to wirelessly transmit a beacon signal within a coverage area associated with an indoor location, the beacon signal including beacon identification information;

the mobile device configured to:  
detect the beacon signal;  
extract the beacon identification information from the detected beacon signal; and  
transmit, to a server via a communication channel separate from the beacon signal, a request including the beacon identification information; and

the server configured to:  
receive the request via the separate communication channel;  
determine the indoor location based at least in part on the beacon identification information;  
select content associated with the determined indoor location; and  
cause the selected content to be transmitted to the mobile device.

## Title

**Indoor Proximity-Marketing Platform Using Multi-Channel Beacon Data Relay and Rule-Based Content Selection**

## Abstract

An indoor proximity-marketing platform includes one or more beacon devices, a portable computing device, and a remote computing system. The portable computing device receives beacon data from a beacon device through a first communication channel and forwards information derived from the beacon data to the remote computing system through a second communication channel different from the first communication channel. The remote computing system determines a location or proximity context associated with the portable computing device based at least in part on the forwarded information. The remote computing system evaluates one or more configured events and rules associated with the location or proximity context, generates or retrieves a result of the evaluation, and selects content based on the location, an identified event, an applicable rule, the result, or a combination thereof. The selected content is transmitted to the portable computing device for presentation or other responsive processing.

## Exemplary Claims

1. **A computer-implemented proximity-content delivery system, comprising:**

   a plurality of beacon devices disposed at respective physical locations within an indoor environment, each beacon device being configured to wirelessly transmit beacon data over a first communication channel;

   a portable computing device comprising a first communication interface configured to receive the beacon data over the first communication channel and a second communication interface configured to communicate over a second communication channel different from the first communication channel; and

   a computing system in communication with the portable computing device over the second communication channel, the computing system comprising at least one processor and memory storing instructions that, when executed by the at least one processor, cause the computing system to:

   receive, from the portable computing device over the second communication channel, a message comprising at least information derived from beacon data received by the portable computing device over the first communication channel;

   identify, based at least in part on the information derived from the beacon data, a configured location associated with at least one of the beacon devices;

   determine an event associated with receipt of the beacon data or presence of the portable computing device relative to the configured location;

   evaluate one or more configured rules applicable to the event and the configured location;

   determine a result of evaluating the one or more configured rules;

   select content based at least in part on one or more of the configured location, the event, the one or more configured rules, or the result; and

   transmit the selected content to the portable computing device over the second communication channel.

2. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the first communication channel comprises a short-range wireless broadcast channel and the second communication channel comprises a network connection using a wireless local-area network, a cellular network, or a combination thereof.

3. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the beacon data comprises at least one of a beacon identifier, a location identifier, a campaign identifier, a major identifier, a minor identifier, a transmission-power value, a timestamp, or authentication data.

4. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the information derived from the beacon data further comprises a received-signal-strength measurement, an estimated distance, a device-generated timestamp, or a detected-beacon history.

5. **The system of claim 1**, wherein identifying the configured location comprises mapping a beacon identifier to a location record defining at least one of a building, floor, zone, department, aisle, room, display, or point of interest.

6. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the event comprises at least one of entry into a zone, exit from a zone, continued presence within a zone, movement between zones, proximity exceeding a threshold, proximity falling below a threshold, detection of a sequence of beacon devices, or expiration of a dwell-time threshold.

7. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the one or more configured rules comprise at least one condition relating to a user attribute, device attribute, time interval, inventory state, prior interaction, purchase history, campaign state, frequency limit, consent state, location sequence, or dwell time.

8. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the result comprises at least one of an eligibility determination, a ranked content identifier, a campaign selection, a suppression instruction, a discount value, a recommendation, a notification instruction, or a destination resource identifier.

9. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the selected content comprises at least one of an advertisement, offer, coupon, product recommendation, informational message, navigation instruction, media item, interactive interface, or uniform resource locator.

10. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the instructions further cause the computing system to suppress transmission of the selected content when a configured frequency limit, exclusion rule, consent requirement, or prior-delivery condition is not satisfied.

11. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the portable computing device is configured to present the selected content through an application, operating-system notification, web interface, or digital wallet interface.

12. **The system of claim 1**, wherein the computing system is further configured to:

   receive interaction data indicating an interaction with the selected content;

   associate the interaction data with the configured location, the event, or the result; and

   update at least one rule, campaign metric, user state, or content-selection parameter based on the interaction data.

13. **A computer-implemented method for delivering location-responsive content, the method comprising:**

   receiving, by a portable computing device and over a first communication channel, beacon data transmitted by a beacon device located within an indoor environment;

   generating, by the portable computing device, a message comprising at least information derived from the beacon data;

   forwarding the message from the portable computing device to a computing system over a second communication channel different from the first communication channel;

   identifying, by the computing system and based at least in part on the message, a configured location corresponding to the beacon device;

   determining an event associated with the configured location and the portable computing device;

   selecting at least one configured rule applicable to the event;

   evaluating the at least one configured rule to produce a result;

   selecting content based at least in part on the configured location, the event, the at least one configured rule, and the result;

   transmitting the selected content from the computing system to the portable computing device over the second communication channel; and

   causing the portable computing device to present the selected content.

14. **The method of claim 13**, further comprising determining a proximity state based on a plurality of signal-strength measurements obtained from transmissions of the beacon device.

15. **The method of claim 13**, further comprising determining that the portable computing device has remained associated with the configured location for at least a configured dwell time before selecting the content.

16. **The method of claim 13**, wherein selecting the content comprises:

   identifying a plurality of candidate content items;

   assigning respective scores to the candidate content items according to the result and contextual information associated with the portable computing device; and

   selecting a candidate content item having a score satisfying a selection criterion.

17. **The method of claim 13**, further comprising storing a record associating at least a device identifier, a beacon identifier, the configured location, the event, the result, and an identifier of the selected content.

18. **The method of claim 13**, wherein the message excludes a direct personal identifier and comprises a pseudonymous device or session identifier.

19. **A non-transitory computer-readable medium** storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors of a portable computing device, cause the portable computing device to:

   monitor a first communication channel for beacon data transmitted by one or more beacon devices;

   receive beacon data from a detected beacon device over the first communication channel;

   generate a relay message comprising information derived from the received beacon data;

   transmit the relay message to a remote computing system over a second communication channel different from the first communication channel;

   receive, from the remote computing system over the second communication channel, content selected according to a configured location associated with the detected beacon device, a detected event, at least one configured rule, and a result of applying the at least one configured rule; and

   cause the received content to be presented by the portable computing device.

20. **The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 19**, wherein the instructions further cause the portable computing device to aggregate beacon data received during a time window and include the aggregated beacon data in the relay message.

21. **The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 19**, wherein the instructions further cause the portable computing device to verify authenticity of the beacon data before transmitting the relay message.

22. **The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 19**, wherein the instructions further cause the portable computing device to cache the relay message when the second communication channel is unavailable and transmit the cached relay message after the second communication channel becomes available.
